e Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Please Select... Menu Close Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Online A.S. in Nursing (Rapid City Campus) A.S. in Nursing (Sioux Falls Campus) Degree Completion Mitchell Scholars Program Summer Courses Internships Academic Calendar Academic Catalogs Admissions For Parents & Families Scholarships & Financial Aid Tuition & Fees Visit Campus New Student Registration The First Year Experience International Students Transfer Students Request Information Meet Our Admissions Staff Student Life Academic & Career Services Center Graduate Studies Student Handbook Office of Disability Services Student Handbook Student Life Staff Student Services Title IX TRIO Student Support Services Alumni & Giving Alumni & Giving Giving Alumni President’s Circle Blue & White Days Wesleyan Today Alumni Magazine Advancement Staff About DWU Why DWU Why DWU DWU History Mission & Values Accreditation DWU Facts News Events Who We Are Board of Trustees President’s Office and Cabinet Leadership Council Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map About Mitchell Consumer Information FAQs Our Services DWU Store McGovern Library For Employers Employment at DWU Hold Your Events at DWU McGovern Center for Leadership and Public Service The Kelley Center for Entrepreneurship instagram facebook twitter linkedin Tutoring, Advising, Job Support Academic & Career Services We're here to help you find and use your strengths. Your Strengths. Our Vision. Our Academic and Career Services Center is here to help you find and use your strengths, connect your talents with your educational goals and give you the clarity\n        and focus you need to succeed well after you graduate from DWU. We can also help you choose your major, find the tutoring you need, land an internship and more. The Academic and Career Services Center is in the McGovern Library\n        so be sure to check us out when you visit! Choosing a Major Choosing your major is one of the most important\n        decisions you will make in your education. By selecting a combination of programs, you can truly design a path of learning that is entirely your own. The Academic and Career Services Center\n        can help you explore your options and find the right fit for you. Tutoring DWU provides peer tutoring to all DWU students at no cost. We are also always looking for student tutors who are interested in building up their resumés and gaining real-world work experience with this great\n        experience. Internships and Part-time Jobs The Academic and Career Services Center is here to help you find the internship or part-time job you need to get a rich learning experience and be successful in your future career. Visit\n        our Job and Internship posting page to browse current openings or make an\n        appointment with a career advisor for personalized support by contacting us . Help Finding a Job After Graduation Whether preparing for your first job or exploring new\n        opportunities after graduation, we are here to help. Make\n        an appointment with a career advisor for personalized support by contacting us . This\n        service is available to current DWU students and DWU alumni. Get started today! Activity Fair Our Academic and Career Services Center facilitates an annual DWU Welcome Fest, which introduces DWU\n        students to all that the community of Mitchell has to offer. It also provides an opportunity for businesses to seek part-time employees and volunteers and is a valuable event for everyone who\n        attends. Questions? Get in touch with our Academic Success Coordinator Phone: 605-995-2904 Email: ascs@dwu.edu 1200 W. University Ave. Mitchell, SD 57301 605-995-2600 Contact Us instagram facebook twitter linkedin flickr youtube © 2026 Dakota Wesleyan University Website By morweb.org Student Central Wesleyan Central Campus Map McGovern Library Academic Catalog Academic Calendar About Us COVID-19 Information Privacy Policy"
